					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/captain-kirby" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3440103); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3440103&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606380118" alt="Captain Kirby" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3440103)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/captain-kirby" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3440103); return false;" >Captain Kirby</a></span> <span class="odate time_1550946833 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">23 Feb 2019 18:33</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4163034">
									

<p>I'm so happy to finally see this on the site. I mean, ok Captain Kirby embracing an end of death article is literally the least surprising thing ever, but still.</p>
<p>I'm happy with what you did with the exploration log especially. I think it gives a nice addition of flavor to the Akot people in general, which builds the world nicely.</p>
<p>But overall what I really like about this piece takes end of death and makes it feel more grand. Generally, I tend to write this canon from a more personal perspective, focussing on a single character and letting readers extrapolate that character's experiences. I see this approach taken a lot in other EoD stuff as well, which I personally enjoy because I love character based narratives, and I don't want to see that trend stop.</p>
<p>However, this doesn't really take that route. It uses End of Death to tell a story that leans into its sci-fi elements more. The lore and the world wreak of more classical plot-driven science fiction stories, and I love to see that new approach applied to the canon in a way that still fits with the overall bleak and gray vibe that is exemplified in the rest of End of Death.</p>
<p>Also, as a side point - I like the irony of the Foundation essentially writing history reports on the future.</p>
<p>So yeah. Good stuff my man. Good stuff.</p>

							</div>

								
					
